  "name": "Impact on Population Density on Growth Rate of Walleye Pollock in the Aleutian Basin. Bull. Sea Fish. Inst. Gdynia 1991, No. 1-2:22-30.",
  "description": "The otolith presents changes in length, age and girth of Pollock during 6 years of explanation of Pollock stock in Donut Hole. General note of Pollock increased continually between 1985 and 1990\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: Collect the information on the current state of exploited stock of Pollock in international water of the Bering Sea.",
